      "timeZone": "Europe/London"
     },
     "body": "<p>I ran the script and I get a “version not found” error: so on <a href=\"http://main.tf\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">main.tf</a>, line 365, the Linux version should be updated to the latest (\"64bit Amazon Linux 2 v3.5.7 running Docker\"). </p>\n\n<p>It would be good to update the supported database versions in the description - <a href=\"http://variables.tf\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">variables.tf</a>, line 44, something like “postgresql 12.14, mariadb 10.6.10, mysql 8.0.32”. Also, the readme file needs the postgres version updating.</p>",
     "created": "25/Jul/23 12:01 PM",
